From c7ae9c91eea3436a96bb64af33c058a6378c1e1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Kamami <ict.solomonk@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:15:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Enter all timetable data in the Generator; download PDF, Word
 and Excel

The Directorate can now build a term's timetable without any SMARTTT data:

- Create a term here (academic year, semester 1-3, name, dates, version
  line, "to be used from", prepared by), optionally copying a previous
  term's class rows, units and groups.
- Lecture halls (code, building, capacity, type, available, blocked hours)
  and departments (code, name, school, number of lecturers) are entered in
  the Generator and shared by every term.
- Class rows and units can be added, edited and deleted, with the class rows
  that take each unit; a new unit starts as one whole class.
- Every list has "Paste from Excel" (header row, tab- or comma-separated)
  with a downloadable CSV template; bad rows are reported by line.
- Deleting refuses anything still used by a saved timetable.

The solver, drafts, grouping and readiness read the Generator's own data
through the same snapshot shape as before, so the solver is unchanged.
Importing from SMARTTT still works and now also pre-fills lecture halls and
departments.

Downloads: every draft or version as PDF, Word (.docx, an editable A3
landscape table in the Directorate's layout) or Excel (.xlsx), by class row,
lecture hall or department.

Publishing records the Director's approval even when SMARTTT can't be told
(a term created here, or SMARTTT down); the version is flagged "not yet in
SMARTTT". The publish payload now also carries unit, room and class-row codes.

New read-only endpoints for the Timetable Allocator, behind ALLOCATOR_API_KEY:
GET /api/integrations/allocator/terms and
GET /api/integrations/allocator/terms/{id}/sections (units, groups, class
rows with their departments, and published meetings).

Migration 0002 adds rooms, departments and term details, and makes the
SMARTTT ids on terms, class rows and units optional.

